  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Louisiana obligated $131M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year. Award activity includes 1,082 awards with an average award size of $121K. Fiscal-year totals are partial, because current-year totals are fiscal year to date. Historical context shows obligations of $3.7B in FY22, $4.5B in FY23, $3.9B in FY24, $5B in FY25, and $5.9B in FY26, before the FY27 to date total of $131M. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buying agency so far in FY2027 to date with $40.7M in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $32.7M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $25M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations with $44.7M. STRATEGIC STORAGE PARTNERS, LLC. is the largest vendor by obligations with $31M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 federal obligations in Louisiana much smaller than prior years?",
        "body": "Louisiana obligated $131M in FY2027 to date, compared with multi-billion dollar totals in prior fiscal years. Fiscal-year totals are partial because current-year totals are fiscal year to date. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year, reflecting the partial-year snapshot rather than a full fiscal-year comparison."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors are driving FY2027 obligations in Louisiana?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security leads buying agencies with $40.7M, followed by the Department of Energy with $32.7M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $25M. Facilities Support Services is the top industry with $44.7M, and Ship Building and Repairing follows with $26.2M. STRATEGIC STORAGE PARTNERS, LLC. is the top vendor with $31M, and BOLLINGER SHIPYARDS LOCKPORT, L.L.C. is second with $25.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
